MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Start Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - You have done amazing so far! Now, its time to finish the job. Put all the components
    that you have build together to create the final transformer.
  - Feed both the input and output tokens in their own POSITIONAL ENCODER. Don't
    forget to set the weights and biases on each POSITIONAL ENCODER to the correct
    option ('encoder' and 'decoder' weights respectively)
  - After that, feed the input embedding into the ENCODER.
  - Next feed both the output embedding and the result of the ENCODER into the DECODER.
  - Then pass the result into one last NEURAL NETWORK to create the final embedding.
    This embedding contains all the encoded information gathered by the ATTENTION
    mechanisms in the ENCODER and DECODER.
  - Finally, use the PICK LAST factory to select the final row of the embedding matrix.
    This row represents the output token which is most likely to appear next in the
    sequence based on the relationships calculated between the input token sequence.
  - To represent this final row as a list of probabilities, use the SOFTMAX activation
    function to map each value so the total sum of the row counts up to 1. This is
    the final output of the TRANSFORMER.
